<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8607"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 12:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Let&#39;s try an experiment: use this string to state facts and theory derived from facts that pertain ONLY TO WHAT WE KNOW OF CRIME SCENE EVIDENCE. I.E. DO NOT USE BTK&#39;S CLUES OR WHAT WE KNOW OF LATER MURDERS. YOU MAY USE EVIDENCE IN HIS LETTER DESCRIBING THE MURDERS BUT ONLY THE PHYSICAL DESCRIPTION OF THE MURDER SCENE. IGNORE HIS PERSONAL REMARKS. In other words, we know only that four people were murdered and what was apparent at the crime scene that day. ANYTHING CHARLIE OTERO HAS SAID, OR MIGHT REMEMBER, IN WAY OF HIS RECOLLECTION OF THE EVENTS IS ADMISSABLE, AS LONG AS IT IS NOT HERESAY. AND YOU ARE ALLOWED TO ASK HIM OR ANYONE WITH FIRST HAND KNOWLEDGE OF THE CRIME ANY QUESTION YOU LIKE. TRY TO BE TACTFUL PLEASE. SOLVE THIS CRIME, SOLVE ALL THE CRIMES. <BR> <BR>READY, SET, GO. &#40;REMEMBER, THERE IS NO BTK&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8607-->
<!--Post: 8629--><!--Time: 1109255467-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8629"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 6:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great B, I would like to add a crime scene layout as you go thru this so we dont miss anything if that is ok with you? <BR>1. Crime Scene Response <BR>First person to answer call, secure scene <BR>Team leader, photographer/sketch artist/evidence collector arrive <BR>2.Search Procedures <BR>approach the scene <BR>Look for evidence disgarded outside <BR>document everyone who enters the scene <BR>3.Do not touch body <BR>do grid search of scene for evidence <BR>make sure to document everything at the scene, make a sketch and verbal recorded log <BR>4. collect blood samples, dna, clothes..anything used to perpatrate crime <BR>5. look for signs of burglary and theft <BR>ok people lets make a crime scene. On the exact evidence that we are exactly sure of. Do not add any theories, get your information from the case in news etc.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8629-->
<!--Post: 8632--><!--Time: 1109256977-->
